{"va gamaH": [{"id": "vA gamaH", "headword": "वा गमः", "headword_slp1": "vA gamaH", "fold": "va gamaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "Optionally after the verb गम् , the लिङ् and the सिच् beginning with झल् consonants, in the आत्मनेपद , are कित्।\n\nTerms: कित्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा गमः १.२.१३", "१.२.१३", "१.२.१३ वा गमः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA gamaH १.२.१३", "१.२.१३", "१.२.१३ vA gamaH"]}], "va kyasaH": [{"id": "vA kyazaH", "headword": "वा क्यषः", "headword_slp1": "vA kyazaH", "fold": "va kyasaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affixes of the परस्मैपद are used optionally after the denominative verbs ending in the affix क्यष।\n\nTerms: परस्मैपद", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा क्यषः १.३.९०", "१.३.९०", "१.३.९० वा क्यषः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA kyazaH १.३.९०", "१.३.९०", "१.३.९० vA kyazaH"]}], "va liwi": [{"id": "vA liwi", "headword": "वा लिटि", "headword_slp1": "vA liwi", "fold": "va liwi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "ख्याञ् is optionally the substitute of चक्षिङ् when लिट् (Perfect Tense) follows.\n\nTerms: आर्धधातुक-substitutes", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा लिटि २.४.५५", "२.४.५५", "२.४.५५ वा लिटि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA liwi २.४.५५", "२.४.५५", "२.४.५५ vA liwi"]}], "va yO": [{"id": "vA yO", "headword": "वा यौ", "headword_slp1": "vA yO", "fold": "va yO", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "वी is optionally the substitute of अज् when the affix -- अनद्यतने लुट् ३.३.१५ etc. follows.\n\nTerms: युवन्-elision", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा यौ २.४.५७", "२.४.५७", "२.४.५७ वा यौ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA yO २.४.५७", "२.४.५७", "२.४.५७ vA yO"]}], "va BrasaBlasaBramukramuklamutrasitruwilasaH": [{"id": "vA BrASaBlASaBramukramuklamutrasitruwilazaH", "headword": "वा भ्राशभ्लाशभ्रमुक्रमुक्लमुत्रसित्रुटिलषः", "headword_slp1": "vA BrASaBlASaBramukramuklamutrasitruwilazaH", "fold": "va BrasaBlasaBramukramuklamutrasitruwilasaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix श्यन् optionally used in the active voice after the verbs - भ्राश् 'to shine', भ्लाश् 'to shine', भ्रम् 'to whirl', क्रम् 'to walk', क्लम् 'to be sad', त्रस् 'to fear', त्रुट् 'to cut' and लष् 'to desire'.\n\nTerms: श्यन्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा भ्राशभ्लाशभ्रमुक्रमुक्लमुत्रसित्रुटिलषः ३.१.७०", "३.१.७०", "३.१.७० वा भ्राशभ्लाशभ्रमुक्रमुक्लमुत्रसित्रुटिलषः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA BrASaBlASaBramukramuklamutrasitruwilazaH ३.१.७०", "३.१.७०", "३.१.७० vA BrASaBlASaBramukramuklamutrasitruwilazaH"]}], "va Candasi": [{"id": "vA Candasi", "headword": "वा छन्दसि", "headword_slp1": "vA Candasi", "fold": "va Candasi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In the छन्दस् (Vedas) the substitute of हि is optionally treated as not having an indicatory प्।\n\nTerms: छन्दस्", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "In the Vedas, the long vowel may optionally be the single substitute of both vowels in these cases last mentioned.\n\nTerms: संहितायाम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा छन्दसि ३.४.८८", "वा छन्दसि ६.१.१०६", "३.४.८८", "३.४.८८ वा छन्दसि", "६.१.१०६", "६.१.१०६ वा छन्दसि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA Candasi ३.४.८८", "vA Candasi ६.१.१०६", "३.४.८८", "३.४.८८ vA Candasi", "६.१.१०६", "६.१.१०६ vA Candasi"]}], "va ha ca cCandasi": [{"id": "vA ha ca cCandasi", "headword": "वा ह च च्छन्दसि", "headword_slp1": "vA ha ca cCandasi", "fold": "va ha ca cCandasi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "Optionally the affix ह also comes in the छन्दस् (Vedas) after the word किम् in the Locative -7th case as well as other affixes.\n\nTerms: किम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा ह च च्छन्दसि ५.३.१३", "५.३.१३", "५.३.१३ वा ह च च्छन्दसि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA ha ca cCandasi ५.३.१३", "५.३.१३", "५.३.१३ vA ha ca cCandasi"]}], "va bahunan jatipariprasne qatamac": [{"id": "vA bahUnAM jAtiparipraSne qatamac", "headword": "वा बहूनां जातिपरिप्रश्ने डतमच्", "headword_slp1": "vA bahUnAM jAtiparipraSne qatamac", "fold": "va bahunan jatipariprasne qatamac", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix डतमच् (अतम with the elision of the last syllable) comes after किम् , यत् and तत् , optionally when the object is the determining of the one out of many, the question being that of caste. \n\nTerms: डतमच्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा बहूनां जातिपरिप्रश्ने डतमच् ५.३.९३", "५.३.९३", "५.३.९३ वा बहूनां जातिपरिप्रश्ने डतमच्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA bahUnAM jAtiparipraSne qatamac ५.३.९३", "५.३.९३", "५.३.९३ vA bahUnAM jAtiparipraSne qatamac"]}], "va sanjYayam": [{"id": "vA saMjYAyAm", "headword": "वा संज्ञायाम्", "headword_slp1": "vA saMjYAyAm", "fold": "va sanjYayam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The substitution of अनङ् does not optionally take place when the बहुव्रीहि समास is a name.\n\nTerms: अनङ्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा संज्ञायाम् ५.४.१३३", "५.४.१३३", "५.४.१३३ वा संज्ञायाम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA saMjYAyAm ५.४.१३३", "५.४.१३३", "५.४.१३३ vA saMjYAyAm"]}], "va supyapisaleH": [{"id": "vA supyApiSaleH", "headword": "वा सुप्यापिशलेः", "headword_slp1": "vA supyApiSaleH", "fold": "va supyapisaleH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "According to the opinion of आपिशलि, the वृद्धि is optionally the single substitute, when the अ or आ of a preposition is followed by a Demoninative Verb beginning with ऋ।\n\nTerms: संहितायाम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा सुप्यापिशलेः ६.१.९२", "६.१.९२", "६.१.९२ वा सुप्यापिशलेः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA supyApiSaleH ६.१.९२", "६.१.९२", "६.१.९२ vA supyApiSaleH"]}], "va Buvanam": [{"id": "vA Buvanam", "headword": "वा भुवनम्", "headword_slp1": "vA Buvanam", "fold": "va Buvanam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The word भुवन may optionally keep its accent in a तत्-पुरुष समास before the word पति denoting 'master' or 'lord'.\n\nTerms: तत्-पुरुष समास", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा भुवनम् ६.२.२०", "६.२.२०", "६.२.२० वा भुवनम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA Buvanam ६.२.२०", "६.२.२०", "६.२.२० vA Buvanam"]}], "va jate": [{"id": "vA jAte", "headword": "वा जाते", "headword_slp1": "vA jAte", "fold": "va jate", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "After a species (with the exception of a word for 'garment or covering') or a time-denoting word or after सुख etc. in a बहुव्रीहि समास the word जात has optionally acute accent (उदात्त) on the final.\n\nTerms: समास end acute-2nd-term", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा जाते ६.२.१७१", "६.२.१७१", "६.२.१७१ वा जाते"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA jAte ६.२.१७१", "६.२.१७१", "६.२.१७१ vA jAte"]}], "va sokasyaYrogesu": [{"id": "vA SokazyaYrogezu", "headword": "वा शोकष्यञ्रोगेषु", "headword_slp1": "vA SokazyaYrogezu", "fold": "va sokasyaYrogesu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "हृद् is optionally substituted for हृदय before the words शोक and रोग or the affix ष्यङ् follow.\n\nTerms: Some Substitution", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा शोकष्यञ्रोगेषु ६.३.५१", "६.३.५१", "६.३.५१ वा शोकष्यञ्रोगेषु"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA SokazyaYrogezu ६.३.५१", "६.३.५१", "६.३.५१ vA SokazyaYrogezu"]}], "va Gosamisrasabdesu": [{"id": "vA GozamiSraSabdezu", "headword": "वा घोषमिश्रशब्देषु", "headword_slp1": "vA GozamiSraSabdezu", "fold": "va Gosamisrasabdesu", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "पद् is optionally substituted for पाद before 1. घोष 2. मिश्र and 3. शब्द।\n\nTerms: Some Substitution", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा घोषमिश्रशब्देषु ६.३.५६", "६.३.५६", "६.३.५६ वा घोषमिश्रशब्देषु"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA GozamiSraSabdezu ६.३.५६", "६.३.५६", "६.३.५६ vA GozamiSraSabdezu"]}], "va sapurvasya nigame": [{"id": "vA zapUrvasya nigame", "headword": "वा षपूर्वस्य निगमे", "headword_slp1": "vA zapUrvasya nigame", "fold": "va sapurvasya nigame", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The lengthening of the penultimate vowel of a अङ्ग (stem) ending in न् , before the affixes of the strong-case, is optional in the छन्दस् (Vedas) when ष precedes such a vowel.\n\nTerms: Lengthening", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा षपूर्वस्य निगमे ६.४.९", "६.४.९", "६.४.९ वा षपूर्वस्य निगमे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA zapUrvasya nigame ६.४.९", "६.४.९", "६.४.९ vA zapUrvasya nigame"]}], "va lyapi": [{"id": "vA lyapi", "headword": "वा ल्यपि", "headword_slp1": "vA lyapi", "fold": "va lyapi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The nasal above the roots (i.e. अनुदात्त ending in a nasal and वन and तनादि) is optionally elided before the Absolutive affix ल्यप्।\n\nTerms: अभीय Rules", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा ल्यपि ६.४.३८", "६.४.३८", "६.४.३८ वा ल्यपि"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA lyapi ६.४.३८", "६.४.३८", "६.४.३८ vA lyapi"]}], "va citavirage": [{"id": "vA cittavirAge", "headword": "वा चित्तविरागे", "headword_slp1": "vA cittavirAge", "fold": "va citavirage", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The ओ of दोष् is optionally replaced by ऊ when the sense is that of the disturbing of the mind.\n\nTerms: ऊ substitution", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["वा चित्तविरागे ६.४.९१", "६.४.९१", "६.४.९१ वा चित्तविरागे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vA cittavirAge ६.४.९१", "६.४.९१", "६.४.९१ vA cittavirAge"]}], "va jfBramutrasam": [{"id": "vA jFBramutrasAm", "headword": "वा जॄभ्रमुत्रसाम्", "headword_slp1": "vA jFBramutrasAm", "fold": "va jfBramutrasam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "ए is optionally substituted f